# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"
msgstr "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Superdense coding is a protocol that, in some sense, achieves a complementary aim to teleportation.\n"
"Rather than allowing for the transmission of one qubit using two classical bits of communication (at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement), it allows for the transmission of two classical bits using one qubit of quantum communication (again, at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang superdense coding ay isang protocol na, sa ilang paraan, nagtatamasa ng layuning kabaliktaran ng teleportation.\n"
"Sa halip na payagan ang pagpapadala ng isang qubit gamit ang dalawang classical bits ng komunikasyon (sa gastos ng isang e-bit ng entanglement), pinapayagan nito ang pagpapadala ng dalawang classical bits gamit ang isang qubit ng quantum na komunikasyon (muli, sa gastos ng isang e-bit ng entanglement).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, we have a sender (Alice) and a receiver (Bob) that share one e-bit of entanglement.\n"
"According to the conventions in place for the lesson, this means that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"
"Alice wishes to transmit two classical bits to Bob, which we'll denote by $c$ and $d$, and she will accomplish this by sending him one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mas detalyadong paraan, mayroon tayong isang nagpapadala (Alice) at isang tumatanggap (Bob) na nagbabahagi ng isang e-bit ng entanglement.\n"
"Ayon sa mga kombensyon sa aralin, nangangahulugang hawak ni Alice ang isang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, hawak ni Bob ang isang qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, at magkasama ang pares na $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ ay nasa estado na $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"
"Nais ni Alice na magpadala ng dalawang classical bits kay Bob, na tatawaging $c$ at $d$, at magagawa niya ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpapadala sa kanya ng isang qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is reasonable to view this feat as being less interesting than the one that teleportation accomplishes.\n"
"Sending qubits is likely to be so much more difficult than sending classical bits for the foreseeable future that trading one qubit of quantum communication for two bits of classical communication, at the cost of an e-bit no less, hardly seems worth it.\n"
"However, this does not imply that superdense coding is not interesting, for it most certainly is.\n"
msgstr ""
"Makatwirang tingnan ang tagumpay na ito bilang mas hindi kawili-wili kaysa sa nagagawa ng teleportation.\n"
"Ang pagpapadala ng mga qubit ay malamang na magiging mas mahirap kaysa sa pagpapadala ng mga classical bit sa mahabang panahon, kaya ang pag-trade ng isang qubit ng quantum na komunikasyon para sa dalawang bits ng classical na komunikasyon, at may kasamang gastos na e-bit pa, ay tila hindi sulit.\n"
"Gayunpaman, hindi ito nangangahulugang ang superdense coding ay hindi kawili-wili, dahil tiyak na kawili-wili ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fitting the theme of the lesson, one reason why superdense coding is interesting is that it demonstrates a concrete and (in the context of information theory) rather striking use of entanglement.\n"
"A famous theorem in quantum information theory, known as *Holevo's theorem*, implies that without the use of a shared entangled state, it is impossible to communicate more than one bit of classical information by sending a single qubit.\n"
"(Holevo's theorem is more general than this.\n"
"Its precise statement is technical and requires explanation, but this is one consequence of it.)\n"
"So, through superdense coding, shared entanglement effectively allows for the *doubling* of the classical information-carrying capacity of sending qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alinsunod sa tema ng aralin, isang dahilan kung bakit kawili-wili ang superdense coding ay ipinakita nito ang isang kongkreto at (sa konteksto ng information theory) medyo kapansin-pansing paggamit ng entanglement.\n"
"Isang kilalang teorema sa quantum information theory, na kilala bilang *Holevo's theorem*, ay nagpapahiwatig na nang walang paggamit ng shared entangled state, imposibleng makipag-communicate ng higit sa isang bit ng classical na impormasyon sa pamamagitan ng pagpapadala ng isang qubit.\n"
"(Mas pangkalahatan ang Holevo's theorem kaysa dito.\n"
"Ang eksaktong pahayag nito ay teknikal at nangangailangan ng paliwanag, ngunit ito ay isa sa mga konsekwensya nito.)\n"
"Kaya, sa pamamagitan ng superdense coding, ang shared entanglement ay epektibong nagpapahintulot ng *pagdoble* ng classical information-carrying capacity ng pagpapadala ng mga qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Protocol {#protocol}"
msgstr "Protocol {#protocol}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following quantum circuit diagram describes the superdense coding protocol:\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na quantum circuit diagram ay naglalarawan ng superdense coding protocol:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/superdense-coding.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/superdense-coding.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In words, here is what Alice does:\n"
msgstr "Sa madaling salita, narito ang ginagawa ni Alice:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $d=1$, Alice performs a $Z$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $d=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr "Kung $d=1$, nagsasagawa si Alice ng $Z$ gate sa kanyang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (at kung $d=0$ ay hindi siya gumagawa).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $c=1$, Alice performs an $X$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $c=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr "Kung $c=1$, nagsasagawa si Alice ng $X$ gate sa kanyang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (at kung $c=0$ ay hindi siya gumagawa).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alice then sends her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ay ipinapadala ni Alice ang kanyang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ kay Bob.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bob does when he receives the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ is to first perform a controlled-NOT gate, with $\\mathsf{A}$ being the control and $\\mathsf{B}$ being the target, and then he applies a Hadamard gate to $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
"He then measures $\\mathsf{B}$ to obtain $c$ and $\\mathsf{A}$ to obtain $d$, with standard basis measurements in both cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ginagawa ni Bob kapag natanggap niya ang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ ay una ay nagsasagawa ng controlled-NOT gate, kung saan ang $\\mathsf{A}$ ang control at ang $\\mathsf{B}$ ang target, at pagkatapos ay nag-aaplay siya ng Hadamard gate sa $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
"Pagkatapos ay sinusukat niya ang $\\mathsf{B}$ para makuha ang $c$ at ang $\\mathsf{A}$ para makuha ang $d$, gamit ang standard basis measurements sa parehong kaso.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Pagsusuri {#analysis}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The idea behind this protocol is simple:\n"
"Alice effectively chooses which Bell state she would like to be sharing with Bob,\n"
"she sends Bob her qubit, and Bob measures to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ideya sa likod ng protocol na ito ay simple:\n"
"epektibong pinipili ni Alice kung aling Bell state ang gusto niyang ibahagi kay Bob,\n"
"ipinapadala ni Alice kay Bob ang kanyang qubit, at sinusukat ni Bob upang malaman kung alin ang Bell state na pinili ni Alice.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, they initially share $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$, and depending upon the bits $c$ and $d$, Alice either leaves this state alone or shifts it to one of the other Bell states by applying $\\mathbb{I}$, $X$, $Z$, or $XZ$ to her qubit\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iyon ay, una silang nagbabahagi ng $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ at depende sa mga bits na $c$ at $d,$ iniiwanan ni Alice ang estado o inililipat ito sa isa sa ibang mga Bell state sa pamamagitan ng pag-aplay ng $\\mathbb{I},$ $X,$ $Z,$ o $XZ$ sa kanyang qubit\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's actions have the following effects on the four Bell states:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga aksyon ni Bob ay may sumusunod na epekto sa apat na Bell state:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be checked directly, by computing the results of Bob's operations on these states one at a time.\n"
msgstr "Maaari itong suriin nang direkta, sa pamamagitan ng pagkalkula ng mga resulta ng mga operasyon ni Bob sa mga estadong ito nang isa-isa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, when Bob performs his measurements, he is able to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
"To verify that the protocol works correctly is a matter of checking each case:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, kapag nagsagawa si Bob ng kanyang mga sukat, nagagawa niyang malaman kung alin ang Bell state na pinili ni Alice.\n"
"Ang pag-verify na tama ang paggana ng protocol ay isang bagay ng pagsuri sa bawat kaso:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 00$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 00\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 00$.\n"
msgstr "Kung $cd = 00$, ang estado ng $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ kapag natanggap ni Bob ang $\\mathsf{A}$ ay $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$. Binabago niya ang estadong ito sa $\\vert 00\\rangle$ at nakukuha ang $cd = 00$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 01$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 01\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 01$.\n"
msgstr "Kung $cd = 01$, ang estado ng $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ kapag natanggap ni Bob ang $\\mathsf{A}$ ay $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle$. Binabago niya ang estadong ito sa $\\vert 01\\rangle$ at nakukuha ang $cd = 01$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 10$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $\\vert 10\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 10$.\n"
msgstr "Kung $cd = 10$, ang estado ng $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ kapag natanggap ni Bob ang $\\mathsf{A}$ ay $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle$. Binabago niya ang estadong ito sa $\\vert 10\\rangle$ at nakukuha ang $cd = 10$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $cd = 11$, then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$. He transforms this state into $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 11$. (The negative-one phase factor has no effect here.)\n"
msgstr "Kung $cd = 11$, ang estado ng $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ kapag natanggap ni Bob ang $\\mathsf{A}$ ay $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$. Binabago niya ang estadong ito sa $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ at nakukuha ang $cd = 11$. (Walang epekto ang negative-one phase factor dito.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding implementation {#superdense-coding-implementation}"
msgstr "Implementasyon ng superdense coding {#superdense-coding-implementation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a simple implementation of superdense coding where we specify the circuit itself depending on the bits to be transmitted. First we'll choose two bits to be transmitted. (Later we'll choose them randomly, but for now we'll just make an arbitrary choice.)\n"
msgstr "Narito ang isang simpleng implementasyon ng superdense coding kung saan tinutukoy natin ang circuit mismo depende sa mga bits na ipapadala. Una, pipiliin natin ang dalawang bits na ipapadala. (Mamaya ay random na pipiliin natin ang mga ito, ngunit sa ngayon ay gagawa lang tayo ng arbitrary na pagpili.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we'll build the circuit accordingly. Here we'll allow Qiskit to use the default names for the qubits: $\\mathsf{q}_0$ for the top qubit and $\\mathsf{q}_1$ for the bottom one.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay itatayo natin ang circuit nang naaayon. Dito ay papayagan natin ang Qiskit na gamitin ang mga default na pangalan para sa mga qubit: $\\mathsf{q}_0$ para sa itaas na qubit at $\\mathsf{q}_1$ para sa ibabang isa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/05ae9b94-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/05ae9b94-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not much is new here, except the `measure_all` function, which measures all of the qubits and puts the results into a single classical register (and therefore having two bits in this case).\n"
msgstr "Hindi masyadong maraming bago dito, maliban sa function na `measure_all`, na sumusukat sa lahat ng mga qubit at inilalagay ang mga resulta sa isang classical register (at kaya ay may dalawang bits sa kasong ito).\n"

