# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we'll create a job using the Aer simulator that runs the circuit a single time for a given input pair $(x,y)$.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay lilikha tayo ng isang job gamit ang Aer simulator na nagpapatakbo ng circuit nang isang beses para sa isang ibinigay na pares ng input $(x,y)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we'll play the game 1000 times and compute the fraction that the strategy wins.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, maglalaro tayo ng 1000 beses at kukuwentahin ang bahagi ng mga laong nanalo ang estratehiya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also define a classical strategy and see how well it works.\n"
"This is just one strategy — others can be tested by changing the code — but it is among the optimal classical strategies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari rin tayong mag-define ng klasikal na estratehiya at tingnan kung gaano ito kagaling.\n"
"Isa lamang itong estratehiya — ang iba ay maaaring subukan sa pamamagitan ng pagbabago ng code — ngunit isa ito sa mga pinakamainam na klasikal na estratehiya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Again let's play the game 1000 times to see how well it works.\n"
msgstr "Muli, maglalaro tayo ng 1000 beses upang makita kung gaano ito kagaling.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Although there's randomness involved, the statistics are very unlikely to deviate too much after 1000 runs. The quantum strategy wins about 85% of the time while a classical strategy can't win more than about 75% of the time.\n"
msgstr "Bagaman may kinalaman ang randomness, malamang na hindi magbago nang husto ang mga estadistika pagkatapos ng 1000 runs. Nananalo ang quantum strategy nang mga 85% ng oras habang hindi kayang manalo ang classical strategy nang higit sa mga 75% ng oras.\n"
